Pull request description (draft):

  Bari (AMTAB) currently has timetable data only. AMTAB publishes real-time data
  as JSON-encoded GTFS-RT (https://amtab.bari.it/images/Servizio_Export_GTFS.pdf).
  This adds a protobuf conversion of that export. IDs are passed through unchanged
  and were checked against the Puglia-Bari static feed (trip_id, route_id, stop_id,
  stop_sequence: 100 % match on a live sample). Converter source:
  https://github.com/elija-7580/Publit-/tree/main/feeds/amtab-gtfsrt. License: the static AMTAB GTFS is published on the Comune di Bari open data
  portal under CC-BY. The real-time export is offered by AMTAB on its
  "OpenMobilityData" page (https://amtab.bari.it/it/openmobilitydata) explicitly
  for app developers, without a separate license. AMTAB is owned by the Comune
  di Bari; under Italian CAD art. 52(2), data published by such bodies without
  an explicit license are considered open data. Entry modelled on the existing
  Sicilia-Messina-ATM realtime entry. Happy to adjust if you prefer written
  confirmation from AMTAB first.
